# Initial Setup's Airspeed page, ported from GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigHWAirspeed.cs.
#
# The claim: Activate shows "Enable" and "Use Airspeed" only for the parameters the vehicle has and
# binds the pin and type combos (ConfigHWAirspeed.cs:18-63); "Enable" writes ARSPD_ENABLE twice -
# the page's handler first (:65-84), then the MavlinkCheckBox's own write, which finds the value
# already held (Controls/MavlinkCheckBox.cs:106-143; ExtLibs/ArduPilot/Mavlink/
# MAVLinkInterface.cs:1647-1651). Each change is proved by the vehicle's echo, and put back.
#
# SITL's copter lists ARSPD_ENABLE 0 and, with the sensor off, none of ARSPD_USE, ARSPD_PIN or
# ARSPD_TYPE: "Use Airspeed" is hidden and both combos stay disabled, as in the C#, so the combos'
# writes are covered by the unit tests in crates/mp-gui/src/config/airspeed.rs.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-airspeed.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760
#
# A run that stops half way can leave ARSPD_ENABLE at 1; the first expectation on it then fails
# until a fresh SITL.

screen params
window 1600x1200
budget 9
# A config.xml of its own, so the "Show me again?" boxes this script clicks are not already
# suppressed by the settings of the machine running it.
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
# RawParamWarning, on the Full Parameter List's Activate (ConfigRawParams.cs:92): "Show me
# again?" unticked, so no later visit asks, and OK.
# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click raw-param-warning-again
click raw-param-warning-ok

# Initial Setup lists the page once every parameter is in (isConnected && gotAllParams,
# InitialSetup.cs:291-294), and here parameters are downloaded when asked for.
click param-download
expect params.held > 1000
expect params.value.ARSPD_ENABLE 0

click tab-setup
expect config.airspeed.active false
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
click setup-page-ConfigHWAirspeed
expect setup.page ConfigHWAirspeed
expect config.airspeed.active true
expect config.airspeed.enabled true
expect config.airspeed.heading Airspeed

# What Activate made of SITL's parameters.
expect config.airspeed.enable unchecked
expect config.airspeed.enable.visible true
expect config.airspeed.enable.enabled true
expect config.airspeed.use.visible false
expect config.airspeed.pin.enabled false
expect config.airspeed.pin.options 14
expect config.airspeed.type.enabled false
expect config.airspeed.write none

# Enable: the handler's write, echoed, then the control's, which finds 1 already held.
click airspeed-ARSPD_ENABLE
expect config.airspeed.enable checked
expect params.value.ARSPD_ENABLE 1
expect config.airspeed.write ARSPD_ENABLE 1 unchanged
expect config.airspeed.writes.pending 0
expect config.airspeed.message none

# And back.
click airspeed-ARSPD_ENABLE
expect config.airspeed.enable unchecked
expect params.value.ARSPD_ENABLE 0
expect config.airspeed.write ARSPD_ENABLE 0 unchanged
expect config.airspeed.message none

# Choosing another page hides this one; it is IActivate only.
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
expect config.airspeed.active false
